Jorgen Grahn wrote:
>
> One thing: robe + spell of magic missile -- what's up with that? Even
> at basic skill it seemed incredibly powerful. One zap could take out a
> balrog. Normally I regard missile as almost useless in the later game
> and only use it on large numbers of weak monsters, like summoned bugs.

Check.  The damage from magic missile gets higher with your level so a
high XP character casts extremely nasty magic missiles.  They get very
deadly on monsters that don't resist them or are not immune to them
completely.  It's like later in the game you should build a table of
which nasty monsters are subject to them and which are immune to them. 
Mow down some with magic missiles, deal with the rest using other
methods.

This matches the player immunity issue that is often discussed.  There's
a list of immunities to acquire and as you do you can handle more and
more situations.  This is that immunity on the monsters' side.


